-- title:
--   Local-ring points of the Igusa scheme: finite chart or pole of j
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number, let $\ell$ be a prime, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ at $\ell$ used throughout and $F$ for the full level-$N$ modular function field, with $j \in F$ its $j$-invariant. Let $R_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` be the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $R_{\infty} =$ `chartAlgInf N ℓ` the subalgebra of elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) is the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the two inclusions of the middle chart algebra into $R_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and into $R_{\infty}$, with `ιFin`, `ιInf` the resulting morphisms from $\operatorname{Spec} R_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\operatorname{Spec} R_{\infty}$. Let $A$ be a commutative local ring and let $f \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to$ [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme N ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) be a morphism of schemes. The assertion is that at least one of the following holds: there is a ring homomorphism $\alpha \colon R_{\mathrm{fin}} \to A$ with $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\alpha)$ followed by `ιFin`; or there is a ring homomorphism $\alpha \colon R_{\infty} \to A$ with $f$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}(\alpha)$ followed by `ιInf` and, in addition, $\alpha(j^{-1})$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the two-chart factorisation of local-ring-valued points of the Igusa scheme, refined by the statement that in the second case the chart coordinate $j^{-1}$ vanishes at the closed point, i.e. the point is genuinely at a pole of $j$. It is used in the analysis of $A$-points of the modular curve model, for instance when comparing point reductions with cusp charts and when producing factorisations through the $j$-finite chart.
-- source:
